  (W, "Cryptography is the science of transforming data so that its meaning is hidden, so that undetected alteration is prevented, or so that unauthorised use is prevented. The Internet Security Glossary describes it in these terms and adds that if the transformation is reversible, cryptography also deals with restoring the data [SH]. The Mozilla glossary puts it more simply, as the science that studies how to encode and transmit messages securely, and adds that it tackles identification, authentication and data integrity as well as confidentiality [MD]."),
